  "result": "I wrote the test and ran both commands: it passes on the before snapshot and fails on the after snapshot. The failure is the flagged background-color assertion, not a crash: `expected rgb(220, 252, 231), got rgb(254, 202, 202)`.\n\nThe test finds the \"Savings Accounts\" card by its selector (`section:nth-child(3) > div:nth-child(2)`, outside any iframe). It checks that the card's computed `background-color` is still `rgb(220, 252, 231)`, the light green from the before snapshot. That color comes from the card's inline style changing from `#dcfce7` to `#fecaca`. It doesn't check the card's position, because the card moved down 18 px when the main heading was made larger, which was intended.\n\nThe first version found no element on either snapshot because it compared `frames` to a list, but the snapshot stores it as a tuple. I fixed that before the final runs.",
